-- Commutative prefix operators accept literal-first or ref-first operands
-- symmetrically: `+ 1 x` parses the same as `+ x 1`.
--
-- quant-trader rerun9 (assessment doc) hit a transient where
-- `onep=+ 1 contrib` was reported as failing to parse while the
-- operand-swapped `onep=+ contrib 1` worked. On current main both forms
-- parse cleanly and produce identical `BinOp Add(Literal, Ref)` ASTs
-- across every engine — but the friction was real for a persona run, so
-- this example locks the symmetry contract.
--
-- Covers `+`, `*`, `&`, `|` (the four commutatives where order shouldn't
-- matter). `-` and `/` are non-commutative and have their own examples.

-- `+` literal-first vs ref-first.
plus-lit-first x:n>n;+ 1 x
plus-ref-first x:n>n;+ x 1

-- `*` literal-first vs ref-first.
mul-lit-first x:n>n;* 2 x
mul-ref-first x:n>n;* x 2

-- `&` literal-first vs ref-first (booleans).
and-lit-first b:b>b;& true b
and-ref-first b:b>b;& b true

-- `|` literal-first vs ref-first.
or-lit-first b:b>b;| false b
or-ref-first b:b>b;| b false

-- run: plus-lit-first 5
-- out: 6
-- run: plus-ref-first 5
-- out: 6
-- run: mul-lit-first 5
-- out: 10
-- run: mul-ref-first 5
-- out: 10
-- run: and-lit-first true
-- out: true
-- run: and-ref-first true
-- out: true
-- run: and-lit-first false
-- out: false
-- run: or-lit-first false
-- out: false
-- run: or-ref-first false
-- out: false
-- run: or-lit-first true
-- out: true
